<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Universal Postal Union</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1874">1874</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as UPU, General Postal Union</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Universal Postal Union is an international organisation founded by the Treaty of Bern in 1874, under the name General Postal Union, to create a single postal territory for the exchange of international mail. It took its present name in 1878, has its headquarters in Bern and became a specialised agency of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> in 1948. It is among the oldest international organisations.</p></div>
